// Phase 5.1 temporal assertions: `always P;` asserts P is an invariant that
// holds universally. Without a state-transition model, the checkable meaning is
// validity: P must be true for all inputs. Discharged with Z3 like a verify
// block. A true invariant proves; a false one is refuted with a counterexample.
always forall n: int. n >= 0 ==> n + 1 >= 1;

begin
  println("temporal invariant holds");
end
